Done.

**The bug** (`src/sim.ts:43`): population growth was gated on `foodSurplus >= 0`. Since `foodSurplus = foodProduced - foodConsumed`, a settlement that produces exactly as much food as it consumes has `foodSurplus === 0`, which satisfied the condition — so population grew on a break-even turn. The docstring promised growth "if there was a food surplus," which strictly means `> 0`.

**The fix:** `>= 0` → `> 0`. Population now grows only on a genuine surplus.

**Verified:**
- `src/sim.ts` — comparison corrected.
- `npm run test` — 7/7 pass (was 4). Added three `advanceTurn` tests: break-even (no growth), genuine surplus (growth), and deficit (no growth). The original suite never exercised `advanceTurn` at all, so this class of bug was previously untested.
- `npm run typecheck` — clean.

Only `src/sim.ts` and `tests/sim.test.ts` were touched; the fixture/repo was not modified.


